# RESILIENT-372 — native-merge-queue substitute. Serializes the final merge step:
# rebase the OLDEST viable armed PR onto latest origin/main, wait for ITS `verified`
# to go green undisturbed, squash-merge, loop. Because it rebases only the ONE PR it
# is driving (never the whole armed set), other PRs' `verified` is not reset — each
# PR gets a clean pass, exactly like a native merge queue with build concurrency 1.
# GitHub's native merge queue is a paid-plan feature not available on this account
# (docs/process/MERGE_QUEUE_SETUP.md); this is the chosen substitute.
#
# Companion: where this runs, disable chump-armed-rebaser.timer (the parallel
# rebase-everyone organ that was resetting `verified` on every main move).
#
# INFRA-8194 (Phase R R5): placeholder TEMPLATE. __HOME__ / __REPO_ROOT__ are
# resolved per host by `chump node render-unit` (crates/chump-provision) or its
# shell mirror organ_unit_host_rewrite (install-helsinki-atc.sh,
# chump-node-install.sh). No User= line: the renderer injects User=<run-user>
# for a system-scope install only, never for a --user manager (217/USER).
[Unit]
Description=Chump merge-serializer — serialize the final merge step so each PR gets a clean `verified` pass (RESILIENT-372)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=HOME=__HOME__
Environment=CHUMP_REPO_ROOT=__REPO_ROOT__
ExecStart=/bin/bash -lc 'source __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/dispatch/lib/load-provider-auth.env __HOME__/.chump/providers.env 2>/dev/null; exec __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/coord/merge-serializer.sh'
